Standards and public references
-------------------------------
Findings carry identifiers from MITRE CWE and the OWASP Mobile Application Security
Verification Standard (MASVS) and Mobile Top 10. Only identifiers and names are used.
OWASP MASVS and MASTG are published under CC BY-SA 4.0, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/.

Secret formats
--------------
Many services issue tokens in a fixed, public format, so a pattern for one is the
same whoever writes it. Some of the patterns in backend/src/sast/secretFormats.ts are
identical to those in gitleaks (https://github.com/gitleaks/gitleaks, MIT licence,
Copyright (c) 2019 Zachary Rice).

npm dependencies
----------------
The server and console depend on Fastify and its plugins, zod, React and the Fontsource
font packages, all under MIT, ISC, BSD or similar permissive licences. Their licences
are in the packages themselves (node_modules/<package>/LICENSE). Build-only tools
(Vite, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS) are not distributed with a build.

Tools the container image installs
----------------------------------
The Dockerfile downloads, at build time, apktool, jadx and qpdf (Apache-2.0), a Temurin
JDK (GPLv2 with the Classpath Exception), Chromium (BSD and bundled third-party
licences) and apksigner from the Android build-tools (Apache-2.0). They are not part of
this repository. If you publish a built image, include the licences and notices of these
components with it, and check the Android SDK terms for apksigner.

